      "description": "One seat on the centreline in a glasshouse with windows front, both sides and overhead, because a tug pilot spends the day looking at something two metres off the hull. Two hand controllers fly the ship and the arms; a foot bar swaps between them. The four work lights above the roof are on the same switch as the arm the pilot is holding.",
